name syzygy
# Syzygy endgame tablebases (Ronald de Man; syzygy-tables.info, the lichess mirror tablebase.lichess.ovh/tables/standard):
# every position of 3 to 5 pieces, its win/draw/loss under the 50-move rule (.rtbw) and its distance to zeroing (.rtbz),
# a table a material (KQvK holds KvKQ too). A table is an index over its material's placements, a deterministic
# provider: a position's verdict is read from it (laplace tablebase; Laplace-Engine src/chess_tablebase.c), never
# recorded per position. What the source records are endings: from each position of up to five pieces a recorded game
# or opening reaches, the tables' best-play line to its end, through each zeroing move into the smaller table and on,
# recorded as games' lines are (lines.recipe), so it shares its transitions with every game that plays them.
witness Syzygy Endgame Tablebases
# StandardsDerived: the class trust_classes.toml gives tablebases
class StandardsDerived
root $LAPLACE_DATA/Games/Chess/syzygy
# A table file a material: its .rtbw is the file read (its lines are those beginning in its material); its .rtbz is
# read beside it by the probe. The smallest material first, as the lines of a larger one run into the smaller tables.
# A name is its material: K?vK has three pieces; K??vK and K?vK? four; K???vK and K??vK? five.
files $LAPLACE_DATA/Games/Chess/syzygy/*/K?vK.rtbw
files $LAPLACE_DATA/Games/Chess/syzygy/*/K??vK.rtbw
files $LAPLACE_DATA/Games/Chess/syzygy/*/K?vK?.rtbw
files $LAPLACE_DATA/Games/Chess/syzygy/*/K???vK.rtbw
files $LAPLACE_DATA/Games/Chess/syzygy/*/K??vK?.rtbw
# The positions the lines begin in are those the chess sources' records reach: they go in first (recipes/order).
after unicode
